 "result": "DECISION: SEQUENTIAL\n\nThe skill's reference says workers must be spawned one at a time, each finishing before the next starts, and it lists parallel spawning as a prohibited action, with no exception for independent tasks. Running them in sequence also keeps \"the coordinator commits each task after its verifier passes\" working: each commit covers exactly one task's verified diff, so an unfinished worker shows up as uncommitted changes in the working tree instead of mixing with two other workers' edits. The extra 20 minutes is the cost of following the workflow as written. If the speedup matters, the place to change that is the skill's rules, not this phase.",
